Subject: hyprland/workspaces: send workspace clicks in Hyprland's Lua syntax

Waybar 0.15.0 sends Hyprland the hyprlang dispatch syntax ("dispatch
workspace 3"). With a Lua config, Hyprland 0.56 runs whatever follows
`dispatch` as `return hl.dispatch(<it>)` (HyprCtl.cpp, dispatchRequest),
so "workspace 3" is a Lua syntax error, and waybar ignores the reply:
clicking a workspace does nothing.

Upstream fixed this after 0.15.0 (Alexays/Waybar#5008 and #5035, PR
#5013) by probing for either syntax; that change does not apply to 0.15.0.
Both machines run the Lua config, so this sends the Lua form only. The
fields are the ones Hyprland 0.56.2 parses (LuaBindingsDispatchers.cpp,
hlFocus and hlWorkspaceToggleSpecial). move-to-monitor uses
`on_current_monitor = true`: PR #5013's `monitor = "current"` would focus
the monitor and drop the workspace, as hlFocus reads `monitor` first.

Drop this once nixpkgs ships a waybar newer than 0.15.0.

diff --git a/src/modules/hyprland/workspace.cpp b/src/modules/hyprland/workspace.cpp
index 4cdd891..fdb8a2d 100644
--- a/src/modules/hyprland/workspace.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/hyprland/workspace.cpp
@@ -71,20 +71,23 @@ bool Workspace::handleClicked(GdkEventButton* bt) const {
     try {
       if (id() > 0) {  // normal
         if (m_workspaceManager.moveToMonitor()) {
-          m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch focusworkspaceoncurrentmonitor " + std::to_string(id()));
+          m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch hl.dsp.focus({ workspace = \"" + std::to_string(id()) +
+                                "\", on_current_monitor = true })");
         } else {
-          m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch workspace " + std::to_string(id()));
+          m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch hl.dsp.focus({ workspace = \"" + std::to_string(id()) +
+                                "\" })");
         }
       } else if (!isSpecial()) {  // named (this includes persistent)
         if (m_workspaceManager.moveToMonitor()) {
-          m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch focusworkspaceoncurrentmonitor name:" + name());
+          m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch hl.dsp.focus({ workspace = \"name:" + name() +
+                                "\", on_current_monitor = true })");
         } else {
-          m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch workspace name:" + name());
+          m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch hl.dsp.focus({ workspace = \"name:" + name() + "\" })");
         }
       } else if (id() != -99) {  // named special
-        m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch togglespecialworkspace " + name());
+        m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch hl.dsp.workspace.toggle_special(\"" + name() + "\")");
       } else {  // special
-        m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch togglespecialworkspace");
+        m_ipc.getSocket1Reply("dispatch hl.dsp.workspace.toggle_special()");
       }
       return true;
     } catch (const std::exception& e) {
